            <ArticleTitle>Rapid Mechanistic Evaluation and Parameter Estimation of Putative Inhibitors in a Single-Step Progress-Curve Analysis: The Case of Horse Butyrylcholinesterase.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">E1248</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3390/molecules22081248</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Highly efficient and rapid lead compound evaluation for estimation of inhibition parameters and type of inhibition is proposed. This is based on a single progress-curve measurement in the presence of each candidate compound, followed by the simultaneous analysis of all of these curves using the ENZO enzyme kinetics suite, which can be implemented as a web application. In the first step, all of the candidate ligands are tested as competitive inhibitors. Where the theoretical curves do not correspond to the experimental data, minimal additional measurements are added, with subsequent processing according to modified reaction mechanisms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
